---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
import { breadcrumbs } from "../lib/schema";
---
<Base
  title="Telegram Peptide Dealers — Who to Use and Who to Skip"
  description="An honest read on the Telegram peptide dealer market: the four types of seller, what each is good for, and where the scams sit."
  path="/dealers/"
  schema={[breadcrumbs([{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Dealers", url: "/dealers/" }])]}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Market read · No affiliate links</p>
  <h1>Telegram peptide dealers</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    There are four kinds of seller on Telegram and only one of them is worth your money. This page is the
    market read — including where we sit in it, since pretending we are the only option is useless.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The named desk</h2>
  <p>
    A single handle, a channel, years of history, batch COAs, a written reship policy. Slow to reply at peak,
    priced in a band rather than a discount. This is us. It is also the only category where the paperwork exists
    before you pay.
  </p>

  <h2>2. The group-buy channel</h2>
  <p>
    A channel with 10,000 members and a weekly drop. Cheapest per vial, worst per experience: no COA per batch,
    no reship, and a queue. Fine if you already know the molecule and can absorb a loss.
  </p>

  <h2>3. The reseller</h2>
  <p>
    Buys from a desk and marks it up 30 percent. Convenient if they are in your city and hold stock. Ask which
    desk they buy from — most cannot tell you, which tells you something.
  </p>

  <h2>4. The impostor</h2>
  <p>
    Copies a known display name, changes one character in the handle, DMs you first. Takes payment, sends
    nothing, or sends a vial with a batch number that matches no COA. Every scam story you have read is this
    category.
  </p>

  <h2>Where the scams actually sit</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Unsolicited DMs. If they message you first, assume impostor until the handle checks out.</li>
    <li>Prices 40 percent under every band. A different lab, or no lab.</li>
    <li>Payment details from a handle other than the one you were talking to.</li>
    <li>No channel, DM only.</li>
    <li>"COA on arrival." It should exist before payment.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to compare two dealers fairly</h2>
  <p>
    Ask both for the same thing: the COA for the batch, the price for the same quantity, the reship policy, and
    the carrier. Whoever answers all four in one message without a follow-up is the one. Whoever sends a
    screenshot of a price list and nothing else is not.
  </p>

  <p>Run the five checks on us on the <a href="/verify/">verify page</a> before you decide.</p>

  <CTA
    src="/dealers/"
    label="Dealers page"
    heading="Compare us properly"
    body="Ask for a batch COA, a live price, the reship policy and the carrier. We answer all four in one message."
  />
</Base>